    "description": "<p><b>Requires:</b> <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">Walking</a> Locomotion System</p><p><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">Walking</a> droids are usually bipedal, but a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">Walking</a> droid can be built with three or more legs (usually four) to grant the droid extra stability and <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Carrying_Capacity\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Carrying Capacity\">Carrying Capacity</a>. This doubles the cost of the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Walking\" title=\"Walking\">Walking</a> locomotion system, but the droid's <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Carrying_Capacity\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Carrying Capacity\">Carrying Capacity</a> is 50% higher than that of a bipedal droid of the same <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Abilities\" title=\"Abilities\">Strength</a>. In addition, the droid gains a +5 stability bonus on checks to resist attempts to knock it <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Prone\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Prone\">Prone</a>.</p>",
    "cost": "Locomotion System Cost x 2",
    "requires": "Walking Locomotion System"
  },
